A||N||11||fropuff||I need some audio expertise from you...||||1||
Z||000000||fropuff||09-29-2000||12:11 AM||||Hey, I am in need of a stereo system for my 80 Cutlass.  I already took out the very cool AM, and I'm looking at an AM/FM combo.  I also am looking for some new 3 1/2s for the front dash.  I am looking at a Kenwood stereo and some Blaupunkt 3 1/2s.  I don't want to pay a bunch of money for a stereo system in a car that will only last the winter.  Okay, I want to know how I can get some bass.  The only speakers in the car are the 3 1/2s in the front.  I don't want to buy a sub, and I was wondering if it would be acceptable if I got a stereo and speakers.  What do you think?  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||09-29-2000||02:14 AM||||"Acceptable?"  You have my permission. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  And you missed a great opportunity to purchase my one of a kind (OK, so a few more than one were made--sue me) FM convertor a few weeks back.  You could have kept the original AM only stereo (resale value would have been higher).  Luckily for you, I still have it.  I'd be willing to part with it for a small fortune...ummm...I mean a small amount.  Email me if you're interested.<P>As far as the speakers, you could get some reasonably cheap rear deck mounted 6x9 2- or 3-ways.  Back in the '80s (when I grew up) <I>every</I> cool car had them in the back window.  I think Pioneer made them.  All I can remember was that the model #s all seemed to start with "TRX".||||reg||1
Z||000002||DJRice||09-29-2000||06:01 AM||||I got the Pioneer 3-way 6x9s for the back of my Buick for about $99 @ Wal-Mart and they kicked.  With that trunk and a set of 6x9s on the back deck, you will definitely notice the difference.    Any set of 3.5" plastic cone speakers will sound better than what you have, but if you get a decent Pioneer or kenwood set, you should notice some nice high frequencies out of those as well.  I recommend putting in "Bass Blockers" (Frequency specific Filter Capacitors) on the front speakers so as not to kill them with Bass.  Any high power stereo (more than 30 watts per channel) will drive the speakers well.  I would think you could pick up a high power name brand (pioneer, kenwood, alpine, etc.) AM/FM Casette for $99-$150.  <P>If you would like to see whats out there,  <A HREF="http://www.crutchfield.com" TARGET=_blank>www.crutchfield.com</A>  will give you a good idea as to what your speaker options are.  They may have some of the "shaft" style radios still also.  <P>After you look at that, wonder into your local wal-mart and check out what speaker models they have available, also check your local auto parts stores for one of those combo kits that comes with a radio and speakers.  Occasionally you can find a deal in that type of stuff as well.  <P>Hope this helps. <P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"You mean like the back seat of a Volkswagen?"<p>[This message has been edited by DJRice (edited 09-29-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||09-29-2000||09:16 AM||||80 cutlass' had the thin rear deck just like the Grand Prix's (had a GP) you can fit 6X9's but depth is a problem due to the trunk spring. It was originally designed to have 4X10's in the back deck. Actually if you look the holes are already cut out of the metal for a 4X10. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||fropuff||09-29-2000||04:39 PM||||Monkeyman:  I will take that convertor off your hands if the price is right.  Also, does anyone know anything else about the FM convertor kit things?  What would I do about an antenna?  I have the one that is wired into the windsheild.  About the speakers:  I think I will get some 3 1/2s for the front, then see what it's like.  Oreif, I forgot about the metal cutouts.  I noticed them when I was in the trunk aligning it.  When I carpeted the rear dash, I cut around them, thinking there were blown 4x10s underneath.  Oh well.  Monkeyman, can you give me some more information about this corvertor thing?  Also, does anyone know how to install this convertor?  Has anyone used one?  Thanks.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||fropuff||09-30-2000||11:26 AM||||Anybody?  Monkeyman?  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fropuff||10-01-2000||10:39 AM||||Monkeyman!!!  Anybody!!!???  Help me!!!  Thanks.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||fropuff||11-15-2000||08:35 PM||||Monkeyman:  I was wondering if you still had the FM convertor.  The price is fine with me; I will send it tomorrow if you still have it.  I'm only driving it TWO months, so I don't want to buy an FM.  Can you help me out, PLEASE?!??  Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000008||batboy||11-15-2000||11:30 PM||||Fropuff, MM had to be kidding you. Those FM convertors are antiques from the '70s. The sound sucks compared to modern car stereos.||||reg||1
Z||000009||deceler8||11-16-2000||09:51 AM||||Look on EBAY for a Delco radio of that vintage...I recently bought a 2000 Delco Am/FM radio on EBAY for $2...<P>It's a 1.5DIN...just bought it for the knobs.<P>Every GM car of that vintage had the same radio, I believe.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Philphine||11-16-2000||12:19 PM||||depending on your parking brake size and how its adjusted (or if you even use it) you can look for some small surface mount speakers (3-5" single or some with a separate tweeter) and screw them to the kick panel area. that way you don't have to get into the dash. they make good temporary speakers for now and later car installs while you work out something permanent.||||reg||1
Z||000011||fropuff||11-16-2000||05:11 PM||||I went on eBay, and I found a lot, but none look like they would fit.  They look to high to get into the space.  The one I have now is about 7" wide, 2.5" tall, and about 8" deep.  This is a weird size it seems like.  I might have to go to the salvage yard to get one.  I don't want to buy one and not have it fit.  That would suck.  ||||reg||1
